*  APPLY()'ing an OPSYN'd plain-identifier alias to a statically-DEFINE'd target SIGSEGVs, both modes.
*  PRE-EXISTING, found 2026-08-27 (seat06) while verifying hq_C's routing ruling on
*  conform-opsyn-operator-rebind-gz5-fatal; unrelated to and unfixed by that row's cure.
*  Direct APPLY('twice',21) works; only the ALIASED name crashes -- see
*  FINDING-2026-08-27-seat06-opsyn-alias-dispatch-fixed-mode4-had-no-user-call-hook-and-two-more-gaps.md
*  addendum for the traced dispatch sequence (crashes inside the entry_label retry's second
*  rt_call_named_proc("twice", ...) call, in rt_proc_call_c_lex's non-jmp_entry branch, which calls
*  through rt_frame_prep() -- a stub that unconditionally returns NULL).
        DEFINE('twice(x)')                            :(setup)
twice   twice = x + x                                :(RETURN)
setup   OPSYN('double', 'twice')
main    OUTPUT = APPLY('double', 21)
END
